<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">League of San Genesio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1197</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Tuscan League</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The League of San Genesio was an alliance of Tuscan cities, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, Lucca and Siena, formed in 1197 at San Genesio near San Miniato after the death of Emperor Henry VI. Backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a>, it rejected imperial control of Tuscany and ended the old March of Tuscany as a governing unit. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> stayed loyal to the empire and did not join.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/league-of-san-genesio.jpg" alt="League of San Genesio" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vignaccia76 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cappellasangenesio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
